# Shell scripts are executed inside Linux containers via their shebang line — a CRLF line
# ending there (e.g. "#!/bin/sh\r") makes the kernel look for a nonexistent "/bin/sh\r"
# interpreter and fail with a misleading "not found" error. Force LF on checkout regardless
# of any given machine's core.autocrlf setting (this repo is developed on Windows, where
# autocrlf=true silently reintroduces CRLF into the working tree on every checkout).
*.sh text eol=lf
